# Local environment overrides - never commit real secrets.
.env

# Rust / Tauri build output. src-tauri/Cargo.lock IS committed (this is an application, not a
# library - see .claude/NOTES.md's Standing decisions), only the compiled target/ directory isn't.
/src-tauri/target

# Generated only after `tauri android init` / `tauri ios init` are actually run against a real
# toolchain (see .claude/NOTES.md - neither has been run in this sandbox, so these directories
# don't exist yet). Left ignored for now; once generated they are ordinarily committed (they hold
# real native project files a maintainer may hand-edit), so revisit this the first time either
# init command actually runs rather than blindly keeping the ignore.
/src-tauri/gen

# Local per-account SQLCipher search index databases, if this app is ever run with a dev
# --config pointing app-data-dir at a folder inside this repo. The real path is always the OS's
# actual app-data directory, this is only a safety net.
*.sqlite3
*.sqlite3-*
